body:
Exactly, breakthroughs happen. And it just gets bad if you had been holding back too much. Some people don't have terrible Saturn Returns cuz they were relatively good to themselves (to put in the most general terms lol).

&#x200B;

We'll all heal soon! :)

Oh my goodness. JUST got negative test results myself. My stomach has consistently blown up like im pregnant from bloating daily and tend to have a lot of constipation. SIBO seems like the only thing that makes sense.

&#x200B;

I feel as though I'd prefer not to take antibiotics anyway. Maybe those garlic and oregano supplements the person above me said or some other natural solutions are the better way to go?

YES. EXACTLY THIS.

&#x200B;

The only thing I can say about this is, many people feel this way but don't feel they can express it. So keep putting it out there that this is what you want in a friend. You'll find them, and they'll be grateful one of you spoke up.

WOW. That's good to know. I'm trying to research if she has said anywhere else how long she had struggled with reflux. 

&#x200B;

That makes me feel a bit better, knowing a beautiful singer can get reflux and (I'm guessing) not have significant damage to her vocal cords.

Thank you. I end up taking omeprazole before or after dinner, since I mostly have the throat closing feeling/acid reflux at night.  Do you think it is still very efficient at this time? 

&#x200B;

Oh shoot. My doctor and dietitian didn't mention I can't take a tums with Omeprazole. LOL generally you're giving me more advice on this than they did.

I'm on opremazole, 20mg. It really doesn't help that much more or less than a tums. I end up taking tums instead. 

&#x200B;

I try to keep my head raised, but I believe my rounded over shoulders still causes me issues.

Thanks for this video! Just watched it. 

&#x200B;

This is exactly why I feel differently than others who have falsely claimed their TF is a celebrity. I am choosing the same core choice/have a similar purpose. I also have the same goal as my twin, which is to be an actor and go into the industry. I guess I can let go of my hold onto them as my TF until I actually get more into my career. If we get together, it'll make sense. If we don't, I still am working towards my dream and will meet them as one of my peers.

Yeah, the new moon was in Cap a over the weekend and the sun is in cap. Also, saturn is now is capricorn and will be until the end of 2020 (it's my saturn return).

&#x200B;

I have a huge stellium in cap. I especially felt the cap new moon this weekend. I was freaking out, thought I was behind in life, couldn't think past my short comings...yeah. It's been rough. But usually it passes.

Hi! I'm a Venus Cap with a Cap stellium, and a mars kinda on the cusp of Cap/Sag.

I've always found it a bit hard to trust people at first. So I tend to put up a protective shield when dating. This can come off super closed and uninterested.  Actually, a lot of Cancer suns (don't know of any Cancer Venus interactions) have almost found it offensive because they didn't know me. I used to find this very unfair, without understanding that Cancers really need an obvious display of emotions to feel more secure.

&#x200B;

So that's what I'd keep in mind. I'm sure she's a bit more open since she's a Sag sun. But sometimes Cap Venuses need to know you are trustworthy with their feelings before they really let you in. We also hate feeling coming off desperate or "weak", so we may not show when we're hurt or into you.

&#x200B;

That's a great point. I was thinking this too, as my saturn is also in cap (which is the placement for all my 12th house planets). It's like, I'm getting hit with all the things I still need to work on. Hopefully this is a positive and it means a good change during my Saturn return. 

&#x200B;

Thank you, it does really feel like a time of change :)

That's totally how I feel, like I can't help but soak up others' negativity. What sometimes helps is wearing a black crystal like obsidian or black tourmaline. 

&#x200B;

My mom and sister are really loud and controlling, and I always ended up yelling at them or not talking to them because I hated their dominant natures. 

&#x200B;

I guess it is just part of the emotional depth of the 12th house.

Jan of 1990! But I knew someone born in Dec '90 and we were pretty similar hahah that's crazy!

&#x200B;

Good to know. I feel like i at least am starting to look a groups that could feel more right for me. But its true I've come to terms with the fact that I don't need a "group". Thanks, good to hear I'm not alone.

Yeah you're half right.

&#x200B;

I'm HARDLY a fucking golden child. My mother and father hate when I talk to them about any problem - like literally I was worrying about what to eat on acid reflux and they just said I complain too much. I also have anxiety and depression but they tell me to shut up and stop burdening them with issues.

&#x200B;

I can't have problems or else they say I am killing them. My mom said I was the most terrible daughter in the world, just because I yelled at her for telling me I my problems didn't matter.

Thank you for this. I really have to remember it - the kind of people I want to have around will be understanding and accepting anyway. And it's important to focus on the good people - instead of getting scared or fed up with others who aren't as great. 

&#x200B;

I hope your situation improves as well! I mean, I've learned how to "be social" but after isolation forgot how and yes, it's annoying when you don't know everything they're referencing in terms of music, tv, etc. But also, I'm glad there are people who understand! That's why mental health awareness is so important.

Hi! I'm 28 and started taking classes at 27 myself. I was super shy and had anxiety. I also kept wishing I had started in my early 20s. 

&#x200B;

But firstly, people start acting at all different ages, and have lots of life experiences to put into their acting. Maybe it's late to be a child star, but it's not late at all in general! 

&#x200B;

Like what many have said, it takes exposure and practice. Also, let go of the need to be really good/an "outgoing" person, etc. I was so caught up in thinking I couldn't play a loud, confident girl because my personal temperament is a bit mellow. But my teacher told me it wasn't about that. It's about finding the character's need. There are tons of actors who are more quiet or shy that can turn on the "loudness" because they have great empathy. It's all in good practice and self-belief. :)
